<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hesse</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hesse is a region and federal state of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiesbaden">Wiesbaden</a> as its capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> as its largest city. In Roman times it was the land of the Chatti, from whom the name of the Hessians is probably derived. It formed a landgraviate from 1264, later divided into Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>, and the modern state was created in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hesse.jpg" alt="Hesse" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hesse.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
